# Normalise line endings so the repository is byte-identical regardless of platform.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows checks files out with CRLF and every one of them shows
# as modified on a Mac or in CI — reviews fill with whole-file diffs containing no actual
# change, and `git blame` stops being useful. `git add` on this repo was already emitting
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings, which is that drift starting.
#
# `text=auto` means: normalise to LF *in the repository*, check out using the platform's
# native convention. Windows editors still see CRLF locally; only stored content changes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files whose content is not line-oriented. Marking them explicitly stops git from ever
# attempting normalisation, which would corrupt them silently.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# Lockfiles are generated, not written. Collapsing them in diffs keeps a dependency bump
# from burying the code changes it accompanies.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true diff=none
